title: Other changes to a node's file
pid: f7cce2b3-871e-446b-bd24-fc1d5b312642
body: |2-
  A node's files can change in ways no other leaf records
  ('OtherChange', 'server/types/viewnode.rs'). The change-forest finds,
  for each node in both graphs that differs between them, what the
  other leaves leave out ('other_changes_between' in
  'server/diff_view/other_changes.rs', which names every field of the
  node, so a new field must be placed there):
  - its title or body moved between its home and a more private
    section: it gained or lost overPrivateText (a Hoist does this);
  - its attribution changed (a strip, say);
  - an alias it has in both graphs moved to another skgrepo;
  - the members both graphs give one of its six lists (content, forks,
    hidden, aliases, extra IDs, flags) stand in another order;
  - something else the graph holds changed: a list names a member by
    another of its IDs, or became an empty list from none. A node that
    differs between the graphs in a way nothing else finds has this
    one, so every node that changed records a leaf.
  Together they are one leaf of the node, its other changes
  ('NodeAspect::OtherChanges'), recorded in its home file and drawn as
  one change viewnode ("What each kind of change looks like"). Its
  fingerprint hashes, for each of them, the values it compares
  ('hash_other_changes_values'): each graph's overPrivateText; each
  graph's attribution; the skgrepos of the aliases both graphs give it;
  the order of the members both graphs give the list; for anything
  else, its four lists whole. So a later change of the same kind
  unmarks it, and a change another leaf records (a member added to a
  reordered list, say) does not. A new or deleted node has none: its
  existence leaf covers its files.
